  "releaseNotes": "v0.2.1: Enhanced Integration, Noise Models, and Topological File Format\n- NEW: Topological file format (.tqp) - Human-readable circuit specification with parser and validator\n- NEW: Noise models - Depolarizing, dephasing, amplitude damping, topological error modeling\n- NEW: SU(2)_k anyon theories for extended topological computing capabilities\n- NEW: Algorithm extensions for seamless integration with main package (Grover, QFT, QAOA)\n- NEW: Comprehensive examples (Bell states, fusion, backend comparison, format demo)\n- NEW: Developer deep-dive documentation with mathematical foundations\n- IMPROVED: Ising anyon theory (Majorana zero modes) - Enhanced stability\n- IMPROVED: Fibonacci anyon theory - Optimized performance\n- IMPROVED: Modular data with rigorous Pentagon/Hexagon consistency validation\n- IMPROVED: Topological backend adapter with better error handling\n- IMPROVED: Circuit optimization with noise-aware compilation strategies\n- ADDED: Architecture documentation explaining topological quantum computing principles\n- ADDED: Universal quantum computation guide for gate approximation\n- Status: 451+ tests passing, ready for Azure Quantum Majorana hardware (when API available)",
